{"id":"html-2","element_id":"html-2","form_id":"wrapper-4037-1037","parent_group":"","type":"html","options":[],"cols":"12","conditions":[],"wrapper_id":"wrapper-4037-1037","field_label":"Information","variations":"<div class=\"bubbles-foster-information\">\n  <h3>Foster Agreement and Responsibilities</h3>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Foster animals remain under the legal care and ownership of Bubbles Pet Rescue at all times. Every rescue is microchipped and registered under the organisation.</li>\n    <li>Foster animals must not be rehomed, handed over, or transferred to anyone without our prior approval. Unauthorised transfer or loss of contact will result in action through the appropriate authorities.</li>\n    <li>We ask fosters to send weekly photos and short videos; these keep the animal's adoption profile active and help find a permanent home faster.</li>\n    <li>Bubbles Pet Rescue continues promoting your foster for adoption, may share updates publicly, and will coordinate directly with you when an adopter is selected. Anyone interested in adopting must contact Bubbles Pet Rescue to go through the official process.</li>\n    <li>If your circumstances change or you plan to travel, tell us as early as possible (ideally one week's notice) and we will arrange the animal's next steps safely.</li>\n    <li>Foster animals arrive healthy, vaccinated, sterilised, and cleared from isolation unless otherwise agreed. Contact us immediately about any veterinary needs; we coordinate and cover approved medical costs through our partner clinic. We expect attentive care and animals returned in good health.</li>\n    <li>We provide food and basic supplies when donations and stock allow, and appreciate your help with essentials when supplies are limited.</li>\n    <li>Our team is always available on WhatsApp for questions, concerns, and advice, from arrival until adoption.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>"},
